    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0096" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg76"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 706.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            2, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In connexion with your despatch to me, No.
                    834, of the 6th of February, and my No. 608 to you, of the 3d of March, I now
                    have the honor to <pb facs="0097" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/> transmit a copy of Lord
                    Russel’s note to me, of the 19th of May, respecting the steamer
                    Will-o’-the-Wisp. I think I have seen in the newspapers some later notice of her
                    movements as a blockade runner from Bermuda.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d19-a1.xml" xpointer="d19-a1"/>
            </div>
